license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/diegoarz02/censored-gp-santa-barbara"
abstract: "Code and analytical data supporting the article on Bayesian spatial geostatistics with censored data for mapping heavy-metal soil contamination around the Santa Bárbara mercury mine (Huancavelica, Peru): a spatial Gaussian process with an interval-censored (Tobit) likelihood, compared against substitution by half the detection limit and ordinary kriging through spatial block cross-validation and a masking experiment, and used to map concentrations, uncertainty and exceedance probabilities."
keywords:
  - censored data
  - Gaussian process
  - geostatistics
  - Bayesian inference
  - heavy metals
  - soil contamination
  - limit of detection
  - mercury
  - cadmium
  - Peru
